# TASK-260715-vtot05 \u2014 independent re-review 03 results

Date: 2026-08-19
Verdict: changes requested
Route: to-dev

## Material finding

AC5 remains fail-open for compiler-valid indirection and preprocessing forms that the independent-rereview-03 contract explicitly requires. `scripts/relay_supply_chain.py` classifies files fail-closed, but `FORBIDDEN_RUNTIME_PATTERNS` (lines 132-202) and `scan_runtime` (lines 983-1041) inspect raw text with call-shaped regular expressions. The audit accepts runtime sources that compile or preprocess into forbidden process/download surfaces:

- C macro alias: `#include <stdlib.h>`, `#define RUN system`, then `RUN(command)` \u2014 scanner ACCEPTED; `cc -fsyntax-only` exit 0; preprocessing produces `system(command)`.
- C line-spliced identifier: `sys\
tem(command)` with `<stdlib.h>` \u2014 scanner ACCEPTED; `cc -fsyntax-only` exit 0.
- C function pointer: `int (*run)(const char *) = &system; return run(command);` \u2014 scanner ACCEPTED; `cc -fsyntax-only` exit 0.
- Swift process alias: `typealias Runner = Process; let process = Runner()` \u2014 scanner ACCEPTED; `swiftc -typecheck` exit 0.
- Swift Foundation loader reference: `let loader = Data.init(contentsOf:options:); let data = try loader(remoteURL, [])` \u2014 scanner ACCEPTED; `swiftc -typecheck` exit 0.
- Objective-C split dynamic selector: construct `dataWithContentsOf` + `URL:` through `NSSelectorFromString`, then invoke it with `[NSData performSelector:withObject:]` \u2014 scanner ACCEPTED; `clang -fsyntax-only -x objective-c -framework Foundation` exit 0.
- Adjacent C preprocessor probes using aliases/token pasting for `curl_easy_perform` were also scanner ACCEPTED and `cc -E` exit 0 with expansion to `curl_easy_perform(handle)`.

These are concrete bypasses of the enumerated forbidden process/Foundation/libcurl mechanisms, not an objection that arbitrary-language semantic proof is impossible. The documentation and LOGBOOK claim these mechanism classes are rejected, while the current clean audit exits 0 on the fixtures.

Minimal remediation: make the per-language checks reject references/aliases and compiler preprocessing indirection for the enumerated symbols, not only direct call spelling. At minimum cover C escaped-newline splicing, macro aliases/token pasting and address-taking for process/libcurl entry points; Swift `Process` type references and `Data`/`String` initializer references; and Objective-C dynamic/split selector construction/invocation. Prefer a fail-closed lexer/parser or compiler-token/AST stage per recognized language over extending only call-shaped regexes. Add one regression per executable reproduction while preserving the explicit local-file controls and bounded claim.

