LOGBOOK.md-289-### 1858 — libssh2 adapter closes review round 4 cancellation and cleanup gaps (TASK-260715-1ozsb6)
LOGBOOK.md-290-- ROOT CAUSE: Long-lived reads reused the write-credit deadline; the authentication timeout raced a waiter that still joined an independently owned signer; rekey and keepalive deadlines began only after the shared session gate; and canceled upload cleanup inherited task cancellation, causing its cleanup progress handler to close the shared TCP bridge.
LOGBOOK.md-291-- REWORK: Reads now wait without an implicit idle deadline while retaining operation-scoped cancellation. Socket and signer completion waiters let callers detach promptly, while teardown cancels and joins owned work. Rekey uses the earlier of the caller-visible explicit deadline and `SSHRekeyPolicy.timeout` before gate admission; one keepalive may queue behind KEX. EOF takes the per-channel write gate after accepted writes, and uncertain EOF/exec/upload failures run bounded uncancelled channel reset while siblings survive.
LOGBOOK.md:292:- ERROR SHAPE: Engine channel-open rejection is operation-scoped with explicit `unsupported` RFC reason evidence. EOF and exec-exit failures carry channel scope; upload timeout carries operation scope; connection errors remain lane-scoped and fatal. No deferred semantic is fabricated.
LOGBOOK.md-293-- VERIFICATION: `swift test --filter LibSSH2` passes 27 tests/3 suites; `make validate-core` passes 361 tests/31 suites plus build and boundary checks; strict Swift format and diff checks pass; `make validate-libssh2`, source tamper gates, and the dual-architecture extension-safe macOS provider/harness matrix all exit 0. Logs use the task-scoped `*-05.log` names under `.temp/TASK-260715-1ozsb6/`.
