LOGBOOK.md-301-### 1758 — libssh2 adapter loopback conformance closes review round 2 (TASK-260715-1ozsb6)
LOGBOOK.md-302-- ROOT CAUSE: libssh2 keeps channel-open and reply-requiring global-request nonblocking state on the shared session, so actor reentrancy across `EAGAIN` allowed a second open to resume the first open's state. The custom send/receive callback ABI also requires negative socket errors directly; returning `-1` plus `errno=EAGAIN` made ordinary backpressure appear as a disconnect.
LOGBOOK.md-303-- REWORK: A bounded FIFO session-operation gate now holds one permit across every channel-open, client-rekey, and keepalive/global-request `EAGAIN` sequence while independent channel payload I/O remains interleavable. Callback would-block paths return `-EAGAIN`. Timeout adaptation uses structured tasks and joins the losing branch; bridge shutdown marks terminal state, closes the injected connection, cancels and joins every queued service task, and only then discards buffers or frees engine state.
LOGBOOK.md:304:- CONFORMANCE: A serialized macOS loopback fixture starts ephemeral OpenSSH with an in-memory P-256 external signer and proves host-policy-before-credential ordering, approved public-key authentication, direct-tcpip echo, concurrent exec opens, exec/stdin upload, server-rekey traffic survival, manual client rekey, keepalive transmission, five connected read/cancel races, and three successful connect/close resource baselines. The four M3 semantics remain explicit `unsupported` reports owned by `TASK-260728-3cveay`.
