LOGBOOK.md-413-### 1052 — Bumping a contract revision without a procedure that names its live consumers is how one of them ends up authorizing a rejected revision (TASK-260715-ypo7yo, r7)
LOGBOOK.md-414-- ROOT CAUSE: r5 stamped `TASK-260728-q5kjta`'s scope with "revision 2026-07-28.r5". r6 superseded r5 and **re-pointed one of two live consumers**, so the human authorization node named by AC5 went on authorizing the revision verdict 05 had **rejected**. Its mutation set was r6-correct — only the label was wrong. Reviewer verdict 06 F1.
