LOGBOOK.md:1307:- FIX: Cleanup now reuses the publication parent descriptor, opens the displaced directory relative to it with no-follow semantics, verifies the opened `(st_dev, st_ino)`, and removes only the bounded flat relay bundle entries through that owned descriptor. It rechecks the top-level identity before parent-relative `rmdir`; unsupported names and non-regular entries fail closed.
LOGBOOK.md-1308-- VERIFICATION: The exact post-open cleanup race moves stale A aside and installs foreign B at the staging name. Generation fails, B retains its exact inode and marker, A survives, and the published bundle validates. Normal cleanup, symlink refusal, interruption recovery, all 26 Python tests, 4 Swift manifest tests, accepted-archive bundle check, Black, Python compile, and diff checks pass.

